GO-2024-2584 ASA-2024-005 (GHSA-86h5-xcpx-cfqc, slashing evasion during re-delegation, low): the GitHub advisory bounds the affected range at cosmos-sdk <= 0.50.4 and <= 0.47.9, and its fix commit 7dbed2fc0c3ed7c285645e21cb1037d8810372ae is an ancestor of the v0.53.6 this chain builds (GitHub compare v0.53.6...7dbed2fc: behind, ahead_by 0). The Go vulnerability database entry carries no fixed version for the 0.50+ range, so every 0.50+ build is reported; binary mode reports it because x/auth/vesting is wired into the app (app_config.go) and its message server is linked. Re-check at every SDK bump by re-running the compare; this line falls the day the database records the fixed version.
GO-2026-5932 golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is deprecated as a whole package (Fixed in: N/A; the latest x/crypto still ships it). Sole importer in this build: cosmos-sdk crypto/armor.go (EncodeArmor, DecodeArmor). Executable path: keyring ExportPrivKeyArmor, ImportPrivKey and Rename <- client/keys export.go, import.go, rename.go <- `dendrad keys export|import|rename`, the operator's LOCAL CLI. The other traces the scanner lists reach armor's unexported readers through io.Reader interface dispatch, which only armor.Decode/Encode construct. Never a message, a query, ABCI or a peer; no script in this repository calls those commands. Closes the day the SDK's crypto/armor.go stops importing openpgp/armor -- `make govulncheck` re-reads it at every SDK bump, never this line.
